<p> -Primary		1,303	  1,300	  1,300</p>
<p> -Fully diluted	1,353	  1,355	  1,355</p>
<p>(a) Unaudited and subjecct to year-end adjustments.</p>
<p>(b) Amounts computed in accordance with industry practice</p>
<p>of multiplying income from commissions and fees by</p>
<p>6.67.</p>
<p>(c) After giving effect to amounts attributable to</p>
<p>redeemable preferred stock, assumed exercise of</p>
<p>dilutive stock options, shares issuable pursuant</p>
<p>to the company's senior management incentive plan</p>
<p>and assumed conversion of the 8-1/2 convertible</p>
<p>subordinated debentures issued December 1983 (for</p>
<p>fully diluted income per common share).</p>
<p>(d) Excludes non-recurring, non-operating pre-tax</p>
<p>income of about $4.0 million primarily related</p>
<p>to gains on the sale of an equity position in a</p>
<p>non-consolidated subsidiary and the liquidation</p>
<p>of a non-marketable investment security.</p>
<p>Absent such gains, net income would have been</p>
<p>lower by $2.12 million.</p>
<p>--((New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610))</p>
